WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Your career starts the day you walk out of here. Let's make sure you're ready.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Adult CPR: check for responsiveness, call 911, check for breathing, begin
compressions. 30 compressions at 100-120 per minute, 2 inches deep, allowing
full chest recoil. 2 rescue breaths after every 30 compressions. Continue until

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
CPR: Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation. 30 compressions to 2 breaths at 100-120 per
minute.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
AED: Automated External Defibrillator. Analyzes heart rhythm and delivers shock
if needed.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: HVAC technicians work in extreme heat, at
heights, and near electricity. Cardiac events, heat stroke, and electrical shock
are real risks.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 100-120 compressions per minute. And — 2 inches deep with
full recoil

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

